# Implementing Typo Tolerance in Typesense - xeg io
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-04-20, [Read more](https://www.xeg.io/shared-searches/implementing-and-customizing-typo-tolerance-in-typesense-for-improved-search-results-666c14bed0547e705eb6cd7c)

Typesense offers several advanced configurations for controlling typo tolerance behavior:
- **: Defines the maximum number of typos allowed in the search query.
...
- **: Sets the minimum length of tokens to be considered for typo tolerance.
Short tokens (like "a" or "is") are ignored.
The default is 3.**
```
typo_tokens_threshold
```
- **: Sets the minimum length of tokens to allow 1 typo.
Default is 4.**
```
min_len_1typo
```
- **: Sets the minimum length of tokens to allow 2 typos.
Default is 8.**
…
```
const performAdvancedSearch = async (query, queryBy) => {
try {
const result = await client.collections('books').documents().search({
q: query,
query_by: queryBy,
num_typos: 2,
typo_tokens_threshold: 3,
min_len_1typo: 4,
min_len_2typos: 8
});
console.log(result);
return result;
} catch (error) {
console.error('Advanced Search Error', error);
}
};

# exact match and phrase query supported? · Issue #272
created: 2021-05-19, last updated: 2026-04-16, [Read more](https://github.com/typesense/typesense/issues/272)

By **exact match** I mean: the query "Harry Potter" book will force to have Harry and Potter to follow each other (without typo).
...
👋 @bnfd We don't support exact searching yet, but that's on our prioritized feature backlog.
We do support the "-" operator which you can use to exclude specific words in the search query.
...
let rs = await client.collections("39_products").documents().search({
q: "*",
// query_by: "Codigo_Producto",
filter_by: `Codigo_Producto:=12005051`,
// prefix: false,
// pre_segmented_query: true,
// typo_tokens_threshold: 0,
// num_typos: 0,
});
